      "final": "Based on our constraints and the evaluation of the vector databases, **Weaviate** is the most suitable choice. Here's why:\n\n1. **Hybrid Search Capabilities**: Weaviate supports both BM25 and vector search, which is ideal for our requirement of combining traditional keyword search with vector-based similarity search.\n\n2. **Performance**: It offers strong performance with a p95 latency of ~15ms at 10 million vectors and 96% recall, which aligns well with our performance expectations.\n\n3. **Deployment Options**: Weaviate provides both self-hosting options (via Docker/K8s) and a managed cloud option, offering flexibility in deployment that fits our infrastructure needs.\n\n4. **Advanced Features**: The commercial tier of Weaviate includes advanced features that could be beneficial for future scalability and enhanced functionality.\n\nWhile Weaviate has a more complex module system and a GraphQL API that may require some learning curve, these trade-offs are justified by its robust feature set and performance, which align well with our constraints.",
